The line is not fixed: raster_dsl.emp:207-216 lets `stream_pal_region` name `pal_line` 1..3 and only requires `(addr >> 5) == pal_line`; `patchable` (raster_dsl.emp:383-412) adds no line constraint to `offscreen_ship`; Raster_BuildShipEntry (raster.emp:1050) takes the destination from the trailer's own CRAM address word (`move.w 6(a1), d2`). Today the only shipping fire is on line 2 ($48 >> 5 == 2, ojz_effects.emp:651/raster_dsl.emp:1896), which is what makes the hardcode look right. Concrete failure with a line-1 band: the program's pal_dirty_mask is %0010, so bit 1 is re-asserted every frame by Raster_VBlank (raster.emp:594) and line 1 ships fine; bit 2 becomes dirty only when Palette_Compose ORs %1110 (a cross-fade or a global operator, palette.emp:365/373). On a frame with a fade running AND the Critical queue full — the exact conjunction buffers.emp:295-297 names as reachable ("reachable during a fade + heavy art staging") — line 2's enqueue drops, bit 2 stays set, and the line-1 ship is skipped: one frame where the top-of-screen stripe reverts to the untinted base even though the band's own palette line shipped correctly. The converse direction (band's own line dropped, bit 2 clear, ship proceeds) is benign in practice because the ship's 3 words are idempotent over the previous frame's post-ship CRAM. GATE BLINDNESS: this needs (a) a non-line-2 shipping band, which no fixture authors, and (b) a forced Critical-queue drop, which no scene drives; and the observable is CRAM content mid-frame, which the pixel-blind replay net and frame-latched oracle CRAM reads cannot resolve.

