palette.emp:322-325 — "Each
// layer that runs ORs the CRAM lines it changed into d7; the accumulated mask is
// OR'd into Palette_Dirty at the end so Enqueue_Dirty_Buffers ships only the lines
// that moved."  The body (:327-390) never touches d7: the base layer does `move.b Pal_Compose_Lines,d0` / `or.b d0,Palette_Dirty` (:349-350), the fade/operator arms do `ori.b #%1110,Palette_Dirty` (:365, :373), Palette_DoCycle ORs its own mask internally, and there is no write to Palette_Dirty after `.variants`. The inline comment at :332-334 states the rule the header breaks: "Each layer ORs the lines it moved straight into Palette_Dirty (no dirty accumulator is held across the sub-proc calls — they clobber the data registers)" — Palette_DoCycle/DoFade/DoOperator/DoVariants all declare clobbers(d0-d7...). Failure scenario: someone adding a compose layer follows the header, accumulates into d7 and ORs once before `.done`; the first sub-proc call after their OR destroys d7 (Palette_DoVariants clobbers d0-d7), so Palette_Dirty is written with garbage or zero and Enqueue_Dirty_Buffers ships the wrong palette lines — a mid-frame-write latch or a dropped section palette, once per crossing.

ojz_effects.emp:616-620 — "the
// density guard measures band edge to band edge, and channel 0's fire is modelled at 526
// cycles against a 489-cycle line, so it spills about one line past its own. Two lines of
// separation is the margin". Channel 0's fire is `[reg_sh_on(), stream_pal_region($48,0,2,4,3)]` (fx_tint_band, :638). Under the shipped model: SetReg = FETCH 8 + RUNG 16*RUNGS 5 + WORK_REG 12 + TAIL 10 = 110; PalRegion(3 words) = 8 + (16*1 + 18) + 122 + 3*30 + 10 = 264; fire = FIRE_BASE 302 + 110 + 264 = 676 — the same 676 raster_dsl.emp:644 computes for exactly this shape ("302 + 110 + 264 = 676"). 526 is the RETIRED `418 + 36 x stream_words` model (418 + 3*36 = 526), which raster_dsl.emp:938 records as replaced. RASTER_SCANLINE_CYC is 488, not 489 (raster_dsl.emp:973 "488 is used, floored, so the comparison is conservative in the direction that ADMITS"). The guard still passes (676 <= gap 2 * 488 = 976), so this is comment-only — but the readable margin is 300 cycles, not 450, and the fire spills 188 cycles into the next line, not 38.

